<title>USA: Summit Bancorp Q2 shr $0.90 vs $0.80.</title>
<headline>Summit Bancorp Q2 shr $0.90 vs $0.80.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the Quarter Ended June 30:		 1997(A)     1996</p>
<p> Net Income					  $88,875   $ 75,364</p>
<p> Net Income Per Common Share		   $   .90   $    .80</p>
<p> Average Common Shares Outstanding	    98,593     93,574</p>
<p>For the Six Months Ended June 30:</p>
<p> Net income, before restructuring charges $172,040   $143,104</p>
<p> Restructuring charges, net tax (B)	  (16,680)   (69,979)</p>
<p> Net income					 $155,360   $ 73,125</p>
<p>Net Income Per Common Share:</p>
<p> Net EPS before restructuring charges     $   1.75   $   1.52</p>
<p> Restructuring charges, net of tax (B)	  (.17)	(.75)</p>
<p> Net income					 $   1.58	 $.77</p>
<p> Average Common Shares Outstanding	    98,433     93,354</p>
<p> Book Value Per Common Share		  $  21.19    $ 19.39</p>
<p>		    (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: (A) Results include acquisition of B.M.J. Financial.</p>
<p>(B) Q1 1997 includes $26.5 million restructuring charge, ($16.7 million, or $.17 per common share, after tax).</p>
<p>Q1 1996 restructuring charges were $110.7 million ($70.0 million, or $.75 per common share, after tax) for merger-related expenses for Summit Bancorp, Flemington National Bank and Trust Co, and Garden State Bancshares. Also included in the restructuring charges were costs related to the supermarket banking initiative.</p>
